    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-sstv-reciever"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-sstv-reciever</url>
    <title>Fruit Jam SSTV Receiver</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Catch memes as they surf past on the air waves using a USB SDR and the Fruit Jam&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-sstv-reciever'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/637/medium500/sstv_guide_photo.png?1792168687' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use a USB SDR device and your Fruit Jam to receive, decode, save, and display SSTV images. These images are broadcast on parts of the high frequency spectrum by ham radio operators all around the world. Learn how to setup two kinds of cheap antennas that can capture them. Occasionally the ISS does SSTV events as well, if you want to try your hand at capturing photos from space!&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-sstv-reciever'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-10-19T12:56:36Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Tim C</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
