    <updated>2026-11-04T14:45:12-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-text-to-speech"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-text-to-speech</url>
    <title>CircuitPython Text to Speech</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Make your microcontroller talk with Moonshine Klatt and PicoTTS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-text-to-speech'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/629/medium500/6200-12.jpg?1791315993' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Text to speech on the board with two CircuitPython libraries. Moonshine Klatt fits boards with less memory and needs no voice files. It runs on RP2040, ESP32-S3, SAMD51 (M4) and nRF52840 boards. PicoTTS sounds more natural and needs a PSRAM board like the Fruit Jam or Feather RP2350.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-text-to-speech'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-10-19T11:02:16Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Mikey Sklar</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
