    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-face-detection"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-face-detection</url>
    <title>Fruit Jam Face Detection</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;100% offline person detection with CircuitPython&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-face-detection'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/638/medium500thumb/Convert_to_GIF_project_-_October_14__2026_at_13.36.15%281%29.gif?1791999558' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Is someone here? This project can let you know! You can use a Fruit Jam running CircuitPython with a USB webcam to run a local front face detection model from OpenCV and output the camera feed over DVI, When a face is detected, a green box is drawn around the face. This is a great way to add person detection to projects, like a video doorbell, without connecting to The Cloud™️since this runs 100% locally and offline.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-face-detection'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-10-14T17:44:25Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Liz Clark</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4630</id>
    <published>2026-10-02T09:21:23-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T11:40:45-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-sdr-for-am-fm-weather-radio-on-fruit-jam"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-sdr-for-am-fm-weather-radio-on-fruit-jam</url>
    <title>USB Host SDR for AM/FM &amp; Weather Radio on Fruit Jam</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Tune in to FM radio on your Fruit Jam with a USB SDR.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-sdr-for-am-fm-weather-radio-on-fruit-jam'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/630/medium500/fruit_jam_radio_guide_photo.png?1791403621' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Listen to live radio broadcasts from your Fruit Jam, played via the TLV320 DAC's 3.5mm output. Use the on-board buttons or a USB keyboard to control the dials. Save your favorite stations as presets for easy access.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-sdr-for-am-fm-weather-radio-on-fruit-jam'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-10-09T13:19:08Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Tim C</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4632</id>
    <published>2026-10-05T15:53:33-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T14:18:41-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-motion-tracking-eyeballs"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-motion-tracking-eyeballs</url>
    <title>Fruit Jam Motion Tracking Eyeballs</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Turbo-powered motion tracking&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-motion-tracking-eyeballs'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/632/medium500thumb/around.gif?1791394112' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Do you ever feel like someone or something is watching you? In the case of this project, it is! You can use a Fruit Jam running CircuitPython with a USB webcam to display monster eyes that gaze in the direction of motion captured by the webcam. The CircuitPython code utilizes Turbo helper modules to speed up tasks like drawing the monster eyes and checking for new motion in the camera frames.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/fruit-jam-motion-tracking-eyeballs'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-10-09T12:43:36Z</updated>
