    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-turbo-sushi-conveyor-belt"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-turbo-sushi-conveyor-belt</url>
    <title>CircuitPython Turbo Sushi Conveyor Belt</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Speed up your sushi conveyor belt with CircuitPython Turbo&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-turbo-sushi-conveyor-belt'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/627/medium500thumb/shorterBarSolo.gif?1790865876' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Back when the Qualia S3 was first released I wanted to run the sushi conveyer belt animation on one of the long bar displays. I tried the project in CircuitPython, but it was way too slow so I had to use Arduino with PlatformIO. Much like Jiro, I never stopped dreaming of sushi and hoped to one day revisit the project and have it run in CircuitPython. With Turbo, that day has finally come.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-turbo-sushi-conveyor-belt'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-10-02T09:44:54Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Liz Clark</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4597</id>
    <published>2026-08-26T13:08:17-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T13:51:09-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-pov-bike-wheel"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-pov-bike-wheel</url>
    <title>CircuitPython POV Bike Wheel</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Light up your Bike with Persistence of Vision Images&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-pov-bike-wheel'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/597/medium500/pov_bike_wheel_hero.jpeg?1787941806' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Paint glowing pictures in the air with CircuitPython and a spinning bike wheel. Upload dozens of images, and pimp your ride in style.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/circuitpython-pov-bike-wheel'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-09-29T15:59:42Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Erin St Blaine</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4619</id>
    <published>2026-09-14T15:33:56-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T13:24:53-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/pixeldust-digital-sand-for-circuitpython"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/pixeldust-digital-sand-for-circuitpython</url>
    <title>PixelDust Digital Sand for CircuitPython</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Let the grains fall where they may.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/pixeldust-digital-sand-for-circuitpython'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/619/medium500thumb/metro_rp2350_sand_simulation.gif?1789652465' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This demo takes advantage of the CircuitPython Turbo speed up and the Picogame module to render sand particles and simulate gravity and physics. This type of demo used to require C or Arduino level code to look smooth, but now it's possible with CircuitPython.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/pixeldust-digital-sand-for-circuitpython'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-09-29T15:43:32Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Tim C</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4623</id>
    <published>2026-09-17T09:16:46-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T01:35:04-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tcs3448-14-channel-light-color-sensor-breakout"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tcs3448-14-channel-light-color-sensor-breakout</url>
    <title>Adafruit TCS3448 14-Channel Light / Color Sensor Breakout</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;14 channels of light over I2C&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tcs3448-14-channel-light-color-sensor-breakout'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/623/medium500/6525-00.jpg?1789651252' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Adafruit TCS3448 (a.k.a. TCS34488) Multi-Spectral Sensor is a multi-channel spectrometer, which is a special type of light sensor that is able to detect not only the amount of light present but also the amounts of light within different wavelengths. This means that you can use it to detect much better than the human eye is capable of, what color or colors of light is present.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tcs3448-14-channel-light-color-sensor-breakout'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-09-29T10:18:14Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Liz Clark</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4625</id>
    <published>2026-09-23T12:51:28-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T14:33:28-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-camera-on-fruit-jam"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-camera-on-fruit-jam</url>
    <title>USB Host Camera on Fruit Jam</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;If seeing is believing, then you better believe that your Fruit Jam can now take photos with USB cameras.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-camera-on-fruit-jam'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/625/medium500/fruitjam_usbcamera_guidephoto.png?1790353048' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn how to hook up a USB camera to your Fruit Jam and take photos with CircuitPython. You can save them to CPSAVES for copying to a computer, or just view live preview on a DVI display.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/usb-host-camera-on-fruit-jam'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-09-29T10:08:00Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Tim C</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4624</id>
