    <updated>2026-10-05T19:00:21-04:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/handheld-esp32-arcade-machine-ports"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/handheld-esp32-arcade-machine-ports</url>
    <title>Arcade Machine/Console Emulator for ESP32 Handheld</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Play classic arcade games and consoles on a dedicated ESP32 handheld&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/handheld-esp32-arcade-machine-ports'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/620/medium500/gboytv-4783.jpg?1791215046' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can play original arcade ROMs, Game Boy, and NES games on Feather ESP32 v2 emulations of Intel 8080, Z80, and 6502 games -- Space Invaders, Lunar Rescue, Pac-Man, Galaga, Ms. Pac-Man, Donkey Kong, and Burger Time! All with the same Adafruit Arcade Machine library as our Fruit Jam ports.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/handheld-esp32-arcade-machine-ports'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-09-22T12:13:03Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>John Park</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:learn.adafruit.com,2005:Guides::External/4617</id>
    <published>2026-09-11T12:17:57-04:00</published>
    <updated>2026-11-04T08:03:06-05:00</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tsl2585-digital-uva-and-ambient-light-sensor"/>
    <url>https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tsl2585-digital-uva-and-ambient-light-sensor</url>
    <title>Adafruit TSL2585 Digital UVA and Ambient Light Sensor</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;"Three-in-one" light sensor&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tsl2585-digital-uva-and-ambient-light-sensor'&gt;&lt;img src='https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/guides/images/000/004/617/medium500/6524-00.jpg?1789143548' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Adafruit TSL2585 Digital UVA and Ambient Light Sensor is a great "three-in-one" light sensor that  has ambient light sensing, Infrared channel and UVA (315nm-400nm). In particular it's not that common to get UVA narrow-band sensing on an I2C sensor, so this is great for outdoor light monitoring. It can also be used to measure curing lights, blacklights and reptile lamps! &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href='https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-tsl2585-digital-uva-and-ambient-light-sensor'&gt;Learn More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
    <updated>2026-09-22T10:06:55Z</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Liz Clark</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
